            "block_content": "Must have successfully completed a JCAHPO Ophthalmic Assistant training program or be certified by JCAHPO as an Ophthalmic Assistant, or have two (2) years (1,000 hours or more per year) recent experience in conducting objective ophthalmic testing on a regular basis, including, but not limited to, experience in several of the following procedures: visual acuity testing, non-contact or contact tonometry, visual fields testing, lensometry, testing for color deficiency and depth perception or autorefraction.",
